course: dictionary
lesson: 11319
title: Yew: a tree with a very long life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Yews can live well over a thousand years.» Here yew is a tree, an evergreen with dark green, flat needles. Evergreen means it keeps its leaves all year, even in winter.
explain: Read the words around a word to find its meaning. «Some common garden and wild plants, such as foxglove and yew, are poisonous if eaten.» The word poisonous is the clue: a yew can harm you if you eat it. Ask yourself what would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Yew can also mean the wood of the tree, which is hard but bendy. Long ago, English archers used it to make longbows. Phrases such as «a yew hedge» show that yew can describe something made from or growing as this tree.
fact: Yew is a noun: a yew is one tree, and yews are more than one.
fact: «Yews» can live well over a thousand years, so they are among the oldest living trees.
fact: Almost every part of a yew is poisonous, so never eat its needles, seeds or leaves.
fact: «Poisonous» means harmful to eat or drink, and it can hurt people and animals.
fact: Yew wood is hard but bendy, which is why it was once used for longbows.
exercise: «Yews can live well over a thousand years.» What is a yew in this sentence? | A kind of soft grass | *An evergreen tree with dark green needles | A bird that eats berries | A type of rock found in caves
exercise: Find and copy one word that means harmful to eat. | longbow | hedge | *poisonous | churchyard
exercise: Dani says yew is the wood of the tree. Which sentence about yew wood is true? | It is used to make ice cream | It is soft and crumbles in your hands | It grows only in tropical rainforests | *It is hard but bendy, and was once used for longbows
test: «Almost every part of the yew tree is poisonous.» What does poisonous mean? | Very tall and green | Safe to eat with honey | Good for birds to sing near | *Harmful to eat or drink
test: Which phrase shows that a yew can be very old? | Dark green, flat needles | *2,000 years old or more | Red berry-like cones | Used to make a bow
exam: «Birds eat the red flesh of the berry and pass the seed out whole.» What does whole mean here? | *Not broken or cut, complete | Broken into bits | Cooked | Sweet and sticky
